{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-plugins-mirakl-test-and-go-live","reason":"Full independent read confirms the pinned raw SHA-256, all five exact quote substrings at their stated lines, and accepted receipt equality with candidate and suggestions. The source and fixed Q1/Q2 preserve seller synchronization/KYC tests, split payments excluding commissions, capture-reference and original-split refund constraints, separate live configuration and default seller controls without claiming an actual merchant or bank outcome. One modal qualification needs correction: raw line 81 recommends, rather than mandates, a small live-seller payout pilot because real payouts cannot be tested in test. The source's 'explicitly directs' wording and Q2's 'live pilots must verify bank arrival' can read as a required go-live gate; preserve it as Adyen's recommendation and the only environment in which real bank receipt can be checked. The Mirakl Sources anchor and reciprocal suggestion are valid."}
