{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-plugins-mirakl-payouts","reason":"Full 54-line pinned raw read and SHA-256 matched; all five quotes match their line locators, and receipt, candidate and suggestions agree. The source and fixed Q1/Q2 correctly distinguish seller-invoice net payout attempts, success-triggered liable-account commission/fee transfers, 03:00 CET retries, outside-connector balance risk, and operator bank-payout exclusion. One discoverability conflict remains in the proposed route: the existing adyen-mirakl concept says the operator needs to split payment funds among seller balances 'and commission', following the overview raw line 44, while this payout raw line 19 explicitly says a type Commission split is unnecessary because the connector transfers commissions during the payout cycle. A reader asking whether to split commission at pay-in can receive conflicting guidance from the concept and source without the source- and phase-specific qualification."}
